---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import Art from './Art.astro';
interface Props { page: string; }
const { page } = Astro.props;
---
{page === 'internship' && <><section class="tinted section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">FIND YOUR STARTING POINT</p><h2>Different beginnings.<br />A shared direction.</h2></div><p>You don’t need to arrive with the same experience as everyone else. You do need the willingness to practise.</p></div><div class="three-grid">{[['compass','“I’m new to coding.”','Start with the foundations. Learn to express an idea in Python and develop a method for understanding errors.'],['code','“I know a few basics.”','Connect what you already know to a working application. Move from separate exercises to a complete user journey.'],['brain','“I want to build with AI.”','Understand the software around the model: the data, interface, retrieval, evaluation, and decisions that make an AI feature useful.']].map(([icon,title,copy]) => <article class="feature"><span class="feature-icon"><Icon name={icon} /></span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div></div></section><section class="container section two-grid"><Art name="learning-studio" alt="AI-generated conceptual illustration of learners collaborating at a desk" /><div><p class="eyebrow">BEFORE THE FIRST SESSION</p><h2>Make space for<br />steady progress.</h2><ul class="check-list"><li>A laptop you can use for coding and project work</li><li>A reliable connection for learning resources and collaboration</li><li>Time for approximately 12–15 hours of learning and practice each week</li><li>A habit of asking questions, trying ideas, and keeping notes</li></ul><p>Ask the academy about the teaching timetable, delivery arrangements, and software setup before enrolling. You can discuss how the program fits your current semester.</p></div></section></>}
{page === 'career' && <><section class="container section two-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">A SMALL PROBLEM. A BIGGER WAY TO THINK.</p><h2>How would you find<br />a repeated item?</h2><p>Imagine a list of student registrations. You need to identify duplicates. You could compare each entry with every other entry—or keep track of what you’ve already seen.</p><p>The useful learning is in the comparison: what changes as the list grows, what extra storage is needed, and which cases might surprise you?</p><div class="inline-note"><Icon name="message" /><p>Practise explaining your approach before writing the code.</p></div></div><div class="reasoning-board"><p class="eyebrow light">THE PROBLEM-SOLVING LOOP</p>{[['search','Understand the input'],['network','Choose a structure'],['code','Write a clear solution'],['shield','Test the edge cases'],['message','Explain the trade-off']].map(([icon,label],i) => <div><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><Icon name={icon} /><strong>{label}</strong></div>)}</div></section><section class="tinted section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">QUESTIONS WORTH PRACTISING</p><h2>Let your project lead<br />the technical conversation.</h2><div class="question-grid">{['What happens between clicking Save and seeing the result?','How do you know an AI answer is supported by a document?','What did you test when a tool or API failed?','Why did you choose an agent workflow for this step?','What would you improve if more people used this application?','Which decision changed after you tried the first version?'].map(q => <div><Icon name="message" /><p>{q}</p></div>)}</div></div></section></>}
{page === 'about' && <section class="container section two-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">CAPABILITY GROWS THROUGH CONNECTIONS</p><h2>One idea leads<br />to the next.</h2><p>A Python function becomes an API. An API becomes an application. A document collection becomes a knowledge source. A useful response becomes a reviewed next step.</p><p>That connected progression is the heart of this training journey. Students should be able to see why a concept matters and where it fits in something larger.</p><a class="text-link" href="/programs/ai-engineering-internship/curriculum/">Explore the learning approach <Icon name="arrowRight" /></a></div><div class="academy-principles">{[['book','Understand before extending','Make the first version small enough to explain.'],['shield','Question the result','Use tests and evidence to check what the application does.'],['folder','Leave a trail of learning','Keep the code, notes, and decisions that show your progress.']].map(([icon,title,copy]) => <article><Icon name={icon} /><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></div></article>)}</div></section>}
{page === 'enquire' && <section class="tinted section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">MAKE THE CONVERSATION USEFUL</p><h2>A little context goes a long way.</h2><div class="three-grid">{[['users','Where you are now','Share your degree or year of study and how much coding you’ve tried. Being new is a perfectly useful starting point.'],['target','What you hope to build','Tell us which project or AI capability interests you. A rough idea is enough to start the conversation.'],['clock','What fits your schedule','Ask about available arrangements and discuss the time you can set aside around your college commitments.']].map(([icon,title,copy]) => <article class="feature"><span class="feature-icon"><Icon name={icon} /></span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div><p class="caption">An enquiry is a request for information. It does not enrol you in the program.</p></div></section>}
